\description{
Convert full sequences from one notation to another with mzLib's sequence conversion service, one result per input: for example a MetaMorpheus full sequence to Unimod accessions.

Hands each sequence to mzLib's \code{SequenceConversionService} (with ProForma registered) and returns
what mzLib made of it. The main use is MetaMorpheus or mzLib full sequences to Unimod
accessions: \code{[UniProt:N-acetylserine on S]SEQK} becomes \code{[UNIMOD:1]SEQK}. Nothing is converted
in R or in the bridge; every output and every status is mzLib's.
}
\details{
\strong{Choose Unimod, not ProForma, for UniProt-sourced modifications.} mzLib's ProForma target does
not resolve them and writes them back under their mzLib name, with status \code{"converted"}
(mzLib#1401). In ProForma output, treat any bracket that is not a \code{UNIMOD:} term as unresolved.
The \code{pro_forma} column \code{\link{readers_read_records}} gives a \code{.psmtsv} comes from the same serializer
and has the same gap.
}
\value{
An \code{mzlibr_sequence_conversions}:

  - \code{records}, a data.frame with one row per input, in input order: \code{input}, the sequence as
    sent; \code{output}, mzLib's converted sequence, \code{NA} when the row failed; \code{status},
    \code{"converted"} (an output and nothing recorded against it), \code{"converted_with_warnings"} (an
    output, but mzLib recorded a warning, an error or an incompatible item) or \code{"failed"} (no
    output); \code{failure_reason}, mzLib's \code{ConversionFailureReason} or \code{NA} when it recorded none -
