  - \code{source_format} and \code{target_format}, spelled as mzLib registered them; \code{mode}, the handling
    mode used; \code{source_formats} and \code{target_formats}, every notation mzLib has registered.
  - \code{record_count} sequences, of which \code{converted_count}, \code{warned_count} and \code{failed_count} have
    each status; \code{column_names}; and \code{caveats}, what a status does and does not promise.

  The failed and warned rows are \code{records[records$status != "converted", ]}.

